<h2>What do I do for a living?</h2>
<p>I am a front-end developer at Carnegie Mellon University, based in the
	Marketing department. My team is called "Web
	Strategy", and we are responsible for the look and feel of all
	university-managed web pages, as well as the management of the software and
	systems that support it.</p>
<p>I mainly work in Drupal (I'm a certified expert!), but I also work in
	Cascade CMS, which is an enterprise CMS from a company called Hannon Hill.</p>
<p>Right now, we just launched the CMU Miami page. We continue to work through
	feature development and bug fixes for
	existing sites. We're preparing for a new University News site, which is being
	built by a vendor but will be owned by our team.</p>
<p>I've been very busy!</p>

